<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Harun al-Rashid</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 786–809</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Harun al-Rashid was Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> who reigned from 786 to 809. His reign is remembered as a high point of Abbasid prosperity and culture in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> and is immortalised in The Thousand and One Nights. He exchanged embassies with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/harun-al-rashid.jpg" alt="Harun al-Rashid" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 8/9th-century master(s) · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gold_dinar_of_Harun_al-Rashid,_AH_170-193.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
